export anchor HotelNoirStyle:
    number: 422
    screen: TravelPlanner
    name: Hotel noir
    idea: The trip as a dim hotel lobby in black and brass, a wall of deep key boxes where booked legs hold a hanging key, unbooked legs show an empty hook and flights leave a letter, beside a guest register, a weather telegram and a deco framed map, under slanted blind shadows.
    base: dark
    palette:
        lobby: #0b0b0c, the page and the style sheet
        panel: #151515, the guest register and swatch cards
        cubby: #1c1b19, key box interiors and list rows
        wood: #241f18, the key box frame
        line: #34312c, register rules and panel edges
        ink: #f1ede4, text, flight letters and focus
        muted: #b3ada1, captions, labels and Not booked
        brass: #c9a45c, number plates, rules, the meter and the primary button
        brassText: #e3c27e, section labels, keys, Booked and Done
        onBrass: #1a1305, text on brass
    type:
        Display in Didot, Bodoni 72, Bodoni MT, Georgia. Body in Georgia at
        16px, often italic. Labels in Futura, Century Gothic, Avenir Next at
        12 to 13px caps tracked 0.3em in brass. The telegram in Courier New
        at 15px caps. The title 96px at 400, box titles 26px.
    layout:
        A dark lobby with a warm glow at the top left and diagonal pale
        bands from window blinds across the whole screen. A marquee of thin
        and double brass rules with BRIGHTWORK TRIPS widely spaced in the
        middle. A centred title block, The front desk presents in italic,
        Japan in April in a large Didone face, and a spaced caps line with
        three cities, fourteen days and the dates. Below, two columns. The
        left is the key wall, a 3 by 2 grid of deep cubbies in a thick dark
        wood frame, each shaded dark inside with a brass number plate 01 to
        06 on its top edge. Inside, a drawn object sits left of the text.
        Booked Tokyo and Kyoto hold a brass key with a tag, the train and
        Osaka show an empty hook over a dashed square, and both flights show
        a white letter. The text gives the date in caps, the title, the
        detail in italic and a status tag. Two square buttons follow. The
        right column stacks the guest register, rows Guest, Party, Stay and
        Account in italic, a thin brass meter and Front desk checks with
        dotted leaders, then a telegram card with a brass left bar reading
        the weather with STOP between phrases, then a deco double framed map
        with diamond markers for Tokyo, Kyoto and Osaka. Below 1060px the
        register column moves under the wall, then boxes go two across and
        one across at phone width.
    spacing: An 8px unit. 44px round the title, 32px between the key wall and the register and a 6px wooden frame between boxes.
    density: Medium. Six key boxes, one register, a telegram and a small framed map.
    corners: Square throughout. Only the brass number plates round by 2px.
    borders: A thick dark wood frame round every box, double brass rules in the marquee, dotted leaders in the checks and a brass bar on the telegram.
    shadows: Deep inset shade at the top of each box, long drops under the key wall and the register, and diagonal light bands from blinds.
    icons:
        Drawn objects tell state. Booked is a brass key on its hook, Not
        booked an empty hook over a dashed square and a flight a white
        letter, each with a word in a tag, dashed for Not booked. Done is a
        check and To do a dash.
    focus: A 2px ink outline offset 3px, ringed again by a thin brass line.
    tone: A discreet concierge, such as The front desk presents, Key boxes and Check out.
